{"name":"Pacifica","hex":"#4e77a3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pacifica","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in San Mateo County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pacifica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pacifica (statue)","blocks":[{"text":"Pacifica was a statue created by Ralph Stackpole for the 1939–1940 Golden Gate International Exposition held on Treasure Island in the San Francisco Bay. Stackpole's largest sculpture, it towered 81 feet (25 m) over the entrance to the Cavalcade of the Golden West in the Court of Pacifica. The Court of Pacifica was dedicated to the heroic explorers of Pacific Ocean territories. Pacifica was the theme statue for the exposition, representing world peace, neighborliness, and the power of a unified Pacific coast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Pacifica-Statue_CL01.png/330px-Pacifica-Statue_CL01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacifica_(statue)","wikidata":"Q7122797"},{"title":"Pacifica, California","blocks":[{"text":"Pacifica is a city in San Mateo County, California, United States, on the coast of the Pacific Ocean between San Francisco and Half Moon Bay. As of the 2020 census, Pacifica had a population of 38,640."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Pacifica_aerial_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Pacifica_aerial_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacifica%2C_California","wikidata":"Q925925"},{"title":"Pacifica (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Pacifica is an Argentine indie rock duo formed in Buenos Aires in early 2021 by Inés Adam and Martina Nintzel. The project first gained attention for cover versions posted on social media before moving on to original material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Pacifica_%28In%C3%A9s_Adam%2C_Martina_Nintzel%29_-_April_2025.jpg/330px-Pacifica_%28In%C3%A9s_Adam%2C_Martina_Nintzel%29_-_April_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacifica_(band)","wikidata":"Q134861813"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/StackpoleAAK-0327.jpg/500px-StackpoleAAK-0327.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/StackpoleAAK-0327.jpg/500px-StackpoleAAK-0327.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Ralph Stackpole with a model of Pacifica","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStackpoleAAK-0327.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/S%C3%A1nchez_Adobe_exterior_1.JPG/500px-S%C3%A1nchez_Adobe_exterior_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/S%C3%A1nchez_Adobe_exterior_1.JPG/1280px-S%C3%A1nchez_Adobe_exterior_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/S%C3%A1nchez_Adobe_exterior_1.JPG/500px-S%C3%A1nchez_Adobe_exterior_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AS%C3%A1nchez_Adobe_exterior_1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/0080_rocks.jpg/500px-0080_rocks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/0080_rocks.jpg/1280px-0080_rocks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/0080_rocks.jpg/500px-0080_rocks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm